      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-225078",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following Boolean function:\n$f(x_{1}, x_{2}) = max{(x_{1} \\cdot x_{2} + x_{1})mod2, x_{2}}$.\n\nWhich of the following boolean functions are equivalent to $f$?\n\n1. $g_{1}(x_{1}, x_{2}) = max{x_{1}, x_{2}}$\n2. $g_{2}(x_{1}, x_{2}) = (x_{1} + x_{2})mod2$\n3. $g_{3}(x_{1}, x_{2}) = x_{1} \\cdot x_{2}$\n\n*Hint: If $x$ is an integer, then*\n$xmod2 = {0,\\begin{vmatrix}ifxis even, \\\\ 1,\\end{vmatrix}ifxis odd$."
    },
